diff --git a/docs/tech-design-names-parents-seats.md b/docs/tech-design-names-parents-seats.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55bd5c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/tech-design-names-parents-seats.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Edit names, two parents per child, max 6 seats
+
+**Author:** Yaniv Aharon (planned with Claude)  
+**Date:** 2026-10-23  
+**Branch:** `claude/carpool-names-parents-seats`
+
+## Summary
+
+Small fixes before the ~8 families register. Both parents of a child share one family: the picker lists each child once as "שם שם <child>", and any phone that taps it acts for that family, so the second parent never creates a duplicate. A parent can edit the family's name and the child's name in Preferences, and a car's seats top out at 6, where 6 means six seats instead of "6+ / unlimited". Last, the team's standing weekly drives (their sheet of who always drives which leg) are loaded once, so each new week's cars come already filled.
+
+## Context
+- **Second parent today:** tapping the child already binds the phone to the child's family (`claim_child` → `children.parent_id`), and that works. The trap is the label "שם <parent>": a second parent who doesn't see their own name uses "שם/שם שם שם שם", and `join_group` (deduped on parent name + child name) creates a duplicate child.
+- **Names:** no UI edits names. RLS already lets a phone update its own parent row's `display_name` (invite_link_access.sql). `children` has no update grant.
+- **Seats:** the DB already caps the value (`seats in (3,4,5,6)`, init.sql). Only the client is wrong: `SeatsChoice '6+'` maps to `Infinity` in `src/domain/seats.ts`.
+- Decided with the developer: no separate parent identities. A family is one parent row, and both parents' phones bind to it; who of the two actually drives a slot is the family's business.
+
+## Milestones
+- M0: Picker label, edit names, 6-seat cap — needs: none — est: 3h — spec: e2e/second-parent.spec.ts, e2e/names-and-seats.spec.ts
+- M1: Standing drives + families seed — needs: none — est: 4h — spec: e2e/standing-drives.spec.ts
+
+## M0 — Picker label, names, seats
+- **Picker:** `ChildPicker` labels each child **"שם שם <child>"** and drops the "שם <parent>" line (`he.auth.pick`). The flow is unchanged: one tap, `claim_child`. No migration for this part.
+- **Migration** `20261024000000_rename_child.sql`: `grant update (display_name) on children to authenticated`, plus a `children_update_own` policy using `parent_id = current_parent_id()`, with check `group_id = current_group_id()`. Parent names are already covered.
+- **Repository:** a new `renameFamily({ parentId, parentName, childId, childName })` in both the in-memory and Supabase repositories, covered by the shared contract. Supabase runs `update(...).select()` and throws when the update touches 0 rows, so an RLS-filtered rename can't fail silently. It goes through `logged()`.
+- **UI:** a "שם" card at the top of Preferences with `names-parent` and `names-child` inputs (max length `DISPLAY_NAME_MAX_LENGTH`). The existing שם saves the names when they changed, then the preferences. A failure shows the existing `preferences-save-error`. An empty name shows `names-error` in place and saves nothing. No new screen.
+- **Seats:** `SeatsChoice` becomes `'3'|'4'|'5'|'6'`, and `seatCapacity` returns `Number(seats)`. A new `MAX_SEATS = 6` constant also caps a driver with no preferences row; a car with no driver stays unlimited. The test id `seats-6+` becomes `seats-6`. `supabaseMapping` keeps mapping to the column's 6, so no data change is needed. Update QUESTIONS.md #6.
+
+## M1 — Standing drives + families seed
+The team's sheet is a fixed weekly rota: each family drives the same leg every week, with up to two cars per leg. App availability alone wouldn't fill cars, because drives are proposed only when a parent saves Preferences and the weekly auto-assign was deferred (QUESTIONS.md #24). So the rota gets its own table.
+- **Migration** `20261024000001_standing_drives.sql`: `standing_drives(group_id, parent_id, schedule_slot_id, direction, position)`. The PK is `(schedule_slot_id, direction, position)`, where position 0/1 is the sheet's שם 1/שם 2, and `unique (schedule_slot_id, direction, parent_id)` stops one family holding both cars of a leg. FKs cascade, and the parent FK is `(parent_id, group_id)` as elsewhere. RLS: read `group_id = current_group_id()`; writes revoked from anon and authenticated. Rows are written only by the developer's seed, in the SQL editor.
+- `create or replace ensure_practices`: same body, but its base-car insert left-joins `standing_drives` on the practice's slot, direction and position, and sets `driver_id`. That fills only the cars it *creates* (`on conflict do nothing`), so a car a family released for one week stays open, and nothing already in the database changes. Add to the realtime publication.
+- No in-app editor for the rota (out of scope). A family changes a single week with the existing release; the developer edits the table to change the rota.
+- **Families seed** `supabase/families-seed.template.sql`: a do-block filled with **placeholder** names. Real names are never committed (same rule as `production-seed.template.sql`). One row per family: family name, child name, child area. Then one row per standing drive: child name, weekday, direction, car 1/2. Idempotent per child name. A vitest case in the style of `productionSeed.test.ts` applies it to the migrated schema and asserts the families and the filled cars.
+- **README runbook (developer's steps):** set the hosted group's areas to the team's neighbourhoods. The developer has given them; they go only into the hosted SQL, never into the repo. Fix Monday's times in `schedule_slots`: the sheet has שם 15:15 / שם 18:00, the seed has 16:00 / 18:30. Fill and run the families seed. Every child in the seed needs an area; the list the developer gave misses two of the sheet's children and names one child the sheet doesn't have.
+
+## Security model (kept from PR #11)
+No new anon grants. A phone still binds only through the token's group (`claim_child`). It renames only its own family's parent row and children. Standing drives are read inside the group only and are never written by a phone.
+
+## Verification
+**Verifier:** `npm run verify`, which runs lint, typecheck, vitest, and Playwright excluding `@pending`.
+- Unit (vitest, written first in TDD): pglite `migration.test.ts` cases for renaming one's own vs another family's child (0 rows), the length check, `ensure_practices` filling only new cars, and standing drives being unwritable by a phone. Also `seatCapacity('6')`, the no-preferences cap, the repository contract for `renameFamily`, and the families seed test.
+- e2e (written now, tagged `@pending`): `e2e/second-parent.spec.ts`, `e2e/names-and-seats.spec.ts` and `e2e/standing-drives.spec.ts`. Their Supabase cases skip without the local stack (README "Running the invite-link e2e").
+
+## Upgrading an existing deploy (README addition, developer's steps)
+`supabase db push --dry-run` should list the two new migrations; then `supabase db push`, then redeploy. Then update the group's areas and Monday's times, and fill and run `families-seed.template.sql` in the hosted SQL editor. No new env vars or dashboard toggles.
